.TH PATH_SKIP_COMPONENT 3
.SH NAME
path_skip_component \- skip a single path component
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t path_skip_component(const char* " s ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_skip_component
scans the path string
.I s
of length
.I n
to find the length of the first path component.
.PP
The function iterates through the input string until it encounters a path separator character (defined by the system-specific
.BR path_issep )
or reaches the end of the input buffer
.IR n .
.PP
The implementation accounts for multi-byte UTF-8 sequences, ensuring that separators are only detected when they occur as single-byte characters.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes from the start of the string up to, but not including, the first path separator found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_skip (3),
.BR path_skip_separator (3)